<Base title="About HumAIn Logic" description="HumAIn Logic helps everyday people and small businesses use AI calmly: plain-language tool search, AI news, a Job safety tracker and one weekly email.">
<section class="page-head"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">About</span><h1>About HumAIn Logic</h1></div></section>
<div class="container section" style="padding-top:var(--space-6)"><div class="prose">
<p class="lede">HumAIn Logic (say it “human logic”) helps everyday people and small businesses use AI without stress. AI, explained calmly. Find the right tool for the job.</p>
<p>The site has four parts:</p>
<ul>
<li>A <a href="/tools">tool directory</a>. Describe a task in your own words and we match it to tools that can help.</li>
<li>A calm <a href="/news">AI news</a> feed, collected from public sources and always linked to the original.</li>
<li>A <a href="/tracker">Job safety tracker</a> that shows how AI is likely to change common jobs and what you can do about it.</li>
<li><a href="/newsletter">The Sunday Brief</a>, one calm email a week.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Why we exist</h2>
<p>Most AI coverage is hype or fear. We write for people who just want to know what a tool does, what it costs, and whether it is worth their time. Most jobs are changing, not disappearing, and practical help works better than alarm.</p>
<h2 id="promise">Our promise</h2>
<ul><li>No company pays to be listed or ranked higher. There are no sponsored listings.</li><li>If we ever use affiliate links, every one carries a visible “Affiliate link” badge and never changes rankings.</li><li>We always show where facts come from, and when they were checked. If a price isn't confirmed, we say so.</li><li>We label anything written with AI.</li><li>No pop-ups, no fear-bait, no hype. No account needed, and nothing is behind an email wall.</li></ul>
<h2 id="money">How we make money</h2>
<p>Right now, we don't. The site has no ads, no sponsored listings and no affiliate links. If that changes, we will say so on this page first, and the rules above still apply: payment never changes what we list or how we rank it, and every paid link or sponsor is labeled where you see it.</p>
<h2>Who runs it</h2>
<p>HumAIn Logic is an independent project run by Francisco Scaramanga in Rome, New York.</p>
<h2>Get in touch</h2>
<p>Spotted a mistake or a price that changed? Email <a href="mailto:hello@humainlogic.com?subject=Question%20about%20HumAIn%20Logic">hello@humainlogic.com</a> or see <a href="/contact">Contact</a>. To learn how outlooks are set, read <a href="/methodology">How we decide</a>.</p>
</div></div>
